(Fixture for tests/210_scratch_sandbox.vox - proves a program run via
 'run program in scratch' really does receive its scratch path as
 arguments's first, and can use it for file I/O.)
a text called 'scratch path' is arguments's first.
a text called 'file path' is "{'scratch path'}/hello.txt".
open a file for writing called out at 'file path'.
Write "hello from scratch\n" to out.
Close out.
Print "wrote ok".
